      "result": "Q2 behavior-panel pattern report\n\nPanel: 12 participants over 2026-04-21 through 2026-04-27. 6 had already churned or downgraded; 6 stayed active. Figures below are aggregated behavioral signals only.\n\nSleep variance (device Total sleep events, minutes):\n- Churned cohort: 7 recorded nights, mean 451.3 minutes, population stdev 170.2, range 173 to 662.\n- Active cohort: 17 recorded nights, mean 381.2 minutes, population stdev 61.5, range 164 to 470.\nThe churned cohort's nightly duration varies more widely than the active cohort's.\n\nEngagement drop-off (log entries per calendar day):\n- Churned: 2026-04-21: 14, 2026-04-22: 11, 2026-04-23: 5, 2026-04-24: 5, 2026-04-25: 4, 2026-04-26: 4, 2026-04-27: 2.\n- Active: 2026-04-21: 13, 2026-04-22: 12, 2026-04-23: 7, 2026-04-24: 6, 2026-04-25: 5, 2026-04-26: 6, 2026-04-27: 1.\nBoth cohorts record fewer entries after the first two panel days.\n\nFeature-cancellation timing (subscription status dates only):\n- 3 cancellations and 3 downgrades.\n- Dates: Apr 04, Apr 11, Mar 29, Apr 02, Apr 14, Apr 18.\nThose status changes fall before the panel window or on its opening days, ahead of the entry drop after 2026-04-22.\n\n",
