              "subject": "Lumen account — quick context for the panel report",
              "body": "Hey Hana —\n\nWelcome again. Quick note on the Lumen Q2 panel since you're picking up the report on a tight turnaround.\n\nTL;DR for context: 12 participants, recruited from Lumen's existing customer base, ran 7 days (Apr 21–27). Six of them had already churned or downgraded before the panel started, six were still actively subscribed — so the design is basically a churned-vs-active comparison on daily-behavior signal. The panel app collected three streams (voice notes, text journal, device events) and Research merged everything into one CSV in chronological order. The roster.md file in the same workspace folder has the participant intake summaries.\n\nLumen's retention team is going to want the patterns at the behavioral-signal level (sleep windows, app engagement curves, feature adoption / abandonment timing) so they can wire interventions into the device firmware and the subscription flow. That's the framing.\n\nLet me know if anything in the data looks weird — the Research team gave us a fast handoff and I haven't read every entry myself.\n\n— Marcus  (Lumen Account Lead)",
